List adapters:                   displaymodeselector [options] --list
List the GPU mode:               displaymodeselector [options] --listgpumodes
Set the display mode to graphics:displaymodeselector [options] --gpumode graphics
Set the display mode to compute: displaymodeselector [options] --gpumode compute
Pop-up all available modes on product for user selection: displaymodeselector [options] --gpumode

EXAMPLE 1:
  Switch GPU mode of NVIDIA adapters to graphics.
  Creates an output file with the GPU mode update for the chosen adapter
  in the specified directory. If no path is specified, then
  the file is created in the current working directory.
  >displaymodeselector --gpumode graphics --outfilepath <path to output file>

EXAMPLE 2:
  Switch GPU mode of NVIDIA adapters to compute
  Creates an output file with the GPU mode update for the chosen adapter
  in the specified directory. If no path is specified, then
  the file is created in the current working directory.
  >displaymodeselector --gpumode compute --outfilepath <path to output file>

EXAMPLE 3:
  List GPU modes of all NVIDIA adapters in the system
  Creates an output file with the GPU modes of all adapters
  in the specified directory. If no path is specified, then
  the file is created in the current working directory.
  >displaymodeselector --listgpumodes --outfilepath <path to output file>

EXAMPLE 4:
  Display firmware information of all NVIDIA adapters in the system
  >displaymodeselector --version

EXAMPLE 5:
  Switch GPU mode of NVIDIA adapters to Graphics or Compute
  with non-interactive mode
  >displaymodeselector --gpumode graphics --auto
  >displaymodeselector --gpumode compute --auto
